blocks.en:
We evaluate DepthGraft on both dense and sparse MoE Transformers, covering multiple model scales and attention variants.
Our experiments are organized around three questions:
(1) whether the empirical results support the analysis in Sec. 3.2 , i.e., whether DepthGraft can use cross-layer gradients as a structural regularizer to improve downstream performance while preserving the KV-cache and prefill-efficiency benefits of KV sharing;
(2) whether this effect scales to larger models and remains effective across different attention variants;
and (3) whether the cross-layer connectivity and stage-layout choices in Sec. 3.4 are necessary, and how alternative sharing variants behave under the same training and evaluation protocol.

blocks.zh:
我们用密集和稀疏的MOE变形器评估深度,包括多个模型尺度和注意力变体。
我们的实验围绕三个问题:
(1) 经验结果是否支持第3.2节中的分析,即深度引力是否能够使用跨层梯度作为结构调节器来提高下游的性能,同时保留KV共享的KV缓存和预填效率效益;
(2) 这一影响尺度是否适用于较大的模型,是否在不同的关注变量中依然有效;
以及(3) 第3.4节中的跨层连接和相接选择是否必要,以及替代共享变体如何在相同的培训和评价协议下运作。

blocks.en:
Evaluation. We test few-shot performance on a broad downstream suite covering four capability groups:
knowledge and language understanding with MMLU [ 13 ] , MMLU-Pro [ 34 ] , and LAMBADA [ 24 ] ;
reasoning and mathematics with ARC-Challenge [ 6 ] , SIQA [ 28 ] , and GSM8K [ 7 ] ;
code generation with HumanEval [ 5 ] , MBPP [ 3 ] , and OpenCompass LCBench [ 8 ] ;
and Chinese understanding with C-Eval [ 16 ] , CMMLU [ 19 ] , and C3 [ 29 ] .

blocks.zh:
